=2 Walkthrough
Trade enough {p:Crystals} to the {p:Conquest NPC} to raise your Rank bar and unlock the Mission.
* Speak with a {n:Gate Guard} who will instruct you to go to the **Garden** in {z:Chateau d'Oraguille}.
* Head for {z:Chateau d'Oraguille} and go towards (F-8). You will receive a cutscene.
* Return to the {n:Gate Guard} to receive the Mission.
* If you're low level, gather a party and/or use {p:Trusts|Trust}.
** Only players who are on 7-2 or have completed it may enter.
** It is recommended that you bring a BLM and/or a BRD for {p:sleeping|Sleep (Status)} the mobs.
* You will have to reach {z:Horlais Peak}, accessible via travelling through {z:Ghelsba Outpost} and {z:Yughott Grotto}.
** {z:Yughott Grotto} Home Point #1 places you right ouside the entrance to the Peak.
* Once you're there, get ready and enter the BC.
** The fight is against 3 {m:Orcs|Orc} and 2 {m:Warmachines|Orcish Warmachine}:
** {m:Darokbok of Clan Reaper} (Level 68, {p:PLD})
** {m:Derakbak of Clan Wolf} (Level 68, {p:DRG})
** {m:Jagidbod of Clan Reaper} (Level 68, {p:RNG})
** {m:Wolf Clan Warmachine} (Level 68)
** {m:Reaper Clan Warmachine} (Level 68)
** Open the fight with {p:Elemental Seal} + {s:Sleepga II}. Fight the Warmachines first, then the Paladin, the Dragoon and Wyvern, and the Ranger last. A Melee/NIN can pretty easily solo any of the NMs. Prioritize the Warmachines.
* When finished, you'll receive another cutscene, and receive the {@k} {k:Crystal dowser}.
* Head back to {p:San d'Oria} and speak to any Gate Guard to finish the mission.

=2 Notes
This mission can be carefully soloed by BLM/RDM. Kill the Warmachines first, then RNG. If you have problems landing sleep on the PLD, he can be killed next; if there are few issues, keep him alive for Aspir and target the DRG. Ignore the wyvern, you will still exit the BC with a win once all Orcs are dead if the wyvern is still alive: Instead, keep him slept and use for Aspir. Use Gravity and Bind (though do not waste the MP for these on the RNG, obviously, as he still attacks from a distance). Try to silence the PLD to prevent him from curing himself.
